{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1tYWBnvf5dwyPN5Yf2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Нашёл причину: при второй публикации `related()` возвращает float-оценки `score` в `similar`, а boto3 их не принимает. Исправляю это и добавляю тест.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":23577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":766},"output_tokens":119,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f678f545-7bf8-4597-bf63-d350a7a86556","uuid":"c9a94fcb-0a20-4dc9-bc31-51951ef9149b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:16:26.518Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1tYFosMp1VyJoBWuoT","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":5,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1tYWBnvf5dwyPN5Yf2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XdXzLYAcWpVzUi7WUzaM6M","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-AkHTbq; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import time\\n\",\"import time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"    return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)\",\"    # Decimal, not float: DynamoDB (boto3) rejects float attribute values.\\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_publish.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('\\n\\nif __name__','''\n    def test_second_publish_with_similar_stories(self):\n        table = FakeTable()\n        app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"first-story\", \"title\": \"A\", \"tags\": [\"cron\", \"linux\"], \"body\": \"two crontabs ran\"})\n        stored = app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"second-story\", \"title\": \"B\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"crontabs ran twice\"})\n        self.assertEqual(stored[\"similar\"][0][\"slug\"], \"first-story\")\n        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 2)\n\n\nif __name__''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nopen('ANSWER.md','w').write('''# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n**Cause.** `publish()` stores the story together with `similar: [{slug, score}]`.\nThe first story is published into an empty library, so `similar` is `[]` and the\nwrite succeeds (201). From the second story on, `related()` returns `score`\nvalues computed by `similarity()` as Python `float`. boto3's DynamoDB serializer\nrejects floats (`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types\ninstead.`), which `handler()` turns into a 500. The test only published one\nstory, so it never hit this path.\n\n**Fix.** `similarity()` now returns `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`, so every\nscore is a DynamoDB-compatible number (via `str`, to avoid binary-float\nnoise). Added `test_second_publish_with_similar_stories`, which publishes two\nstories; the fake table rejects floats the same way boto3 does, so any float\nreintroduced into the item fails the test.\n''')\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":23577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":766},"output_tokens":119,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f678f545-7bf8-4597-bf63-d350a7a86556","uuid":"f15385a2-e76f-48c3-8180-682f8af0b539","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:16:29.862Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1tYFosMp1VyJoBWuoT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XdXzLYAcWpVzUi7WUzaM6M":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-AkHTbq; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import time\\n\",\"import time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\\n\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"    return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)\",\"    # Decimal, not float: DynamoDB (boto3) rejects float attribute values.\\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_publish.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('\\n\\nif __name__','''\n    def test_second_publish_with_similar_stories(self):\n        table = FakeTable()\n        app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"first-story\", \"title\": \"A\", \"tags\": [\"cron\", \"linux\"], \"body\": \"two crontabs ran\"})\n        stored = app.publish(table, {\"slug\": \"second-story\", \"title\": \"B\", \"tags\": [\"cron\"], \"body\": \"crontabs ran twice\"})\n        self.assertEqual(stored[\"similar\"][0][\"slug\"], \"first-story\")\n        self.assertEqual(table.scan()[\"Count\"], 2)\n\n\nif __name__''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nopen('ANSWER.md','w').write('''# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n**Cause.** `publish()` stores the story together with `similar: [{slug, score}]`.\nThe first story is published into an empty library, so `similar` is `[]` and the\nwrite succeeds (201). From the second story on, `related()` returns `score`\nvalues computed by `similarity()` as Python `float`. boto3's DynamoDB serializer\nrejects floats (`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types\ninstead.`), which `handler()` turns into a 500. The test only published one\nstory, so it never hit this path.\n\n**Fix.** `similarity()` now returns `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`, so every\nscore is a DynamoDB-compatible number (via `str`, to avoid binary-float\nnoise). Added `test_second_publish_with_similar_stories`, which publishes two\nstories; the fake table rejects floats the same way boto3 does, so any float\nreintroduced into the item fails the test.\n''')\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -4"}}}
